                <pb facs="0731" n="681" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg681"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Broadhead to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1894-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27,
                                1894</hi></date>. (Received August 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 49.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    Federal Council has passed a resolution, which is herewith inclosed, that
                    modifies very materially the rules in regard to commutation tax imposed upon
                    persons who are natives of Switzerland, but who have become naturalized in the
                    United States; still it is not by any means all that could be desired on the
                    subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James O.
                    Broadhead.</hi></signed></closer>



